# ── Damage Assessment Agent — vision model ───────────────────────────────────
# Server-side only. Do NOT prefix with VITE_, or the key ships to the browser.
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your key. .env is gitignored.
#
# Fireworks (recommended — the claim flow sends 3 photos, and Fireworks' VLMs
# take up to 30 images per request as base64 data URIs):
AI_BASE_URL=https://api.fireworks.ai/inference/v1
AI_API_KEY=
AI_MODEL=accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k2p5

# An AMD cloud-native / vLLM endpoint speaks the same OpenAI-compatible shape.
# To switch, point these three at it instead — no code change:
# AI_BASE_URL=https://<your-amd-endpoint>/v1
# AI_API_KEY=<your key>
# AI_MODEL=<a vision-capable model served there, e.g. Qwen/Qwen2.5-VL-32B-Instruct>
#
# Leave AI_API_KEY empty and the claim flow falls back to the deterministic
# on-device assessment, and says so in the UI.

# ── Decision ledger signing (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────
# Server-side only. Absent, the ledger signs with the deterministic FNV-1a digest
# and labels itself as a checksum. Set both and lib/sign.server.ts signs the same
# canonical bytes with HMAC-SHA-256 instead — the structure is identical either way.
# LEDGER_SIGNING_KEY=
# LEDGER_SIGNING_KEY_ID=
